# Keeps the build context to the sources the image actually needs. Without this, `COPY . .` in the
# build stage sweeps in the whole working tree: git history, the host's build output, uploaded
# photos and local logs. The final stage only takes /app/publish, so this is about the build stage
# and any exported build cache - and about not shipping a 200MB context to the daemon.
**/.git
**/.gitattributes
**/.gitignore
**/.github
**/.vs
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/bin
**/obj
**/artifacts
**/Logs
**/.photos
**/.gstack
**/*.user
**/*.suo
**/docker-compose*.yml
**/Dockerfile*
**/.dockerignore
**/*.md
